sessionalHymns.text:
As a pillar and sacrifice of the Church of Christ, O father, thou didst most wisely preserve it unshaken by the temptations of the evil one;
for thou didst destroy all the evil works of Nestorius, proclaiming the Mother of God to be the Theotokos.//
Wherefore, having assembled, we honor thee, O divinely blessed Cyril.

ode8.irmos:
Having spread his hands, Daniel closed the lions' jaws in their den;
while the zealously pious youths, girded with virtue,
quenched the power of the fire and cried aloud://
Bless ye the Lord, all ye works of the Lord.

ode9.irmos:
Eve dwelt under the curse of sin because of the infirmity of disobedience;
but thou, O Virgin Theotokos, hast through the Offspring of thy pregnancy blossomed forth blessing upon the world.//
Wherefore, we all magnify thee.
